{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::source_node_id` identifies the criterion's\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node`:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// The node this question is about.\n    fn source_node_id(&self) -> D::NodeId;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation: `Criterion::source_node_id` returns the criterion's source node, meaning the node the criterion is about.\n\n- **SDK test.** `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement. It calls `review().source_node_id()` directly. It asserts the result equals the `node` the `Review` was built with, so a wrong or constant return value would fail. The same test then verifies and stores evidence under that node's evidence path and loads it back through the same node.\n- **Contracts test.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` is also marked. Its test `Review` returns its `source` field from `source_node_id`. The test asserts the verified value's `source_node_id()` is `Node(1)`, and that the loaded record's `source_node_id()` equals the verified value's. This checks the criterion's reported node flows through to the evidence, and the loaded record's id comes from stored evidence rather than from re-running the criterion.\n- **Gaps.** Both tests exercise one node each. The requirement only says the method identifies the criterion's source node, so no further input class changes the obligation. I found no unaddressed obligation, and the only acknowledgments are none.",
